modify the Software;
create Derivative Works;
deploy the Software in development, testing, staging, demonstration, and production environments;
use the Software for Internal Business Use;
use the Software for personal, educational, research, nonprofit, and community purposes;
make the Software available to employees, contractors, and Affiliates acting on Your behalf; and
create and operate Customer-Specific Deployments as permitted by this License.

You may authorize employees and contractors to exercise these rights solely on Your behalf, provided that You remain responsible for their compliance with this License.

Except as expressly permitted by this License, You may not transfer or sublicense Your rights under this License.

4. Permitted Uses
4.1 Personal Use

Individuals may use, study, modify, extend, and operate the Software for personal purposes.

4.2 Educational, Research, and Nonprofit Use

Educational institutions, research organizations, nonprofit organizations, and community groups may use, study, modify, extend, and deploy the Software for their own activities.

This permission does not authorize the Sale of the Software or operation of a Competing Service.

4.3 Internal Business Use

Organizations may:

use the Software in commercial production environments;
adapt the Software to their business requirements;
deploy the Software on-premises;
deploy the Software in public, private, or hybrid cloud environments;
integrate the Software into internal systems and business processes;
use the Software to support products and services offered by the organization;
process information belonging to the organization or its customers;
permit employees and contractors to use the Software on the organization’s behalf; and
permit Affiliates to use the Software for Internal Business Use.

Commercial activity conducted with the assistance of the Software is permitted. This includes using Bridge365 to classify, route, process, analyze, or respond to business communications.

4.4 Customer Projects

Consultancies, system integrators, independent professionals, and other service providers may:

assess customer requirements relating to the Software;
install the Software for customers;
configure the Software for customers;
customize the Software for customers;
develop customer-specific integrations and extensions;
migrate customer data and configurations;
provide training, maintenance, and support;
operate a Customer-Specific Deployment on behalf of a customer; and
charge for these professional services.

A service provider may provide the same professional services to multiple customers. However, each hosted Customer-Specific Deployment must satisfy Section 2.7.

4.5 Integrations and Independent Products

You may create and commercially distribute integrations, connectors, plug-ins, applications, agents, tools, and independent products that interact with the Software, provided that:

they do not include or distribute a substantial portion of the Software contrary to this License;
they are not presented as an authorized or official Bridge365 product without written permission;
they do not circumvent the restrictions of this License; and
they do not constitute a Competing Service.
5. Explicitly Permitted Commercial Services

For clarity, You may charge for:

consulting;
architecture and design services;
implementation;
installation and configuration;
system integration;
custom development;
customer-specific extensions;
data migration;
training and workshops;
maintenance;
technical support;
security and compliance assessments;
monitoring and operational support; and
operation of a Customer-Specific Deployment.

These activities are permitted when the primary value being sold is the professional service and not access to, redistribution of, or licensing of the Software itself.

Merely describing a professional service as “managed” does not automatically make it prohibited. The actual nature of the service determines whether it is an allowed Customer-Specific Deployment or a prohibited Competing Service.

6. Restrictions

Unless You have received prior written permission from the Licensor, You may not perform any of the activities described in this section.

6.1 Sale of the Software

You may not:

Sell the Software;
charge a license fee for the Software;
charge a distribution fee for the Software;
sublicense the Software for compensation;
bundle the Software into a commercial offering whose primary or substantial value is the Software itself; or
make access to the Software the principal item being purchased.

Reasonable charges for physical media, bandwidth, or pass-through infrastructure costs must not be used to circumvent this restriction.

6.2 Sale of Derivative Works

You may not:

Sell a Derivative Work;
charge a license fee for a Derivative Work;
sublicense a Derivative Work for compensation;
Sell a fork of the Software;
repackage and Sell the Software or a Derivative Work under another name; or
make superficial modifications for the purpose of avoiding this License.
6.3 Competing Hosted and Managed Services

You may not:

offer the Software or a Derivative Work as a Competing Service;
provide a shared or multi-tenant Hosted Service based substantially on the Software;
provide customers with paid access to a substantial set of the Software’s features or functionality;
offer a white-label Hosted Service based substantially on the Software; or
enable another person or entity to conduct any of these activities.

Operation of a Customer-Specific Deployment is permitted when it complies with Sections 2.7, 4.4, and 5.

6.4 White-Label Distribution

You may not rebrand the Software or a Derivative Work and distribute, license, or market it as Your own standalone software product.

This restriction does not prevent a service provider from applying customer-specific visual branding to a permitted Customer-Specific Deployment, provided that:

Bridge365 copyright and license notices remain intact;
the deployment is not represented as software owned by the service provider or customer;
the Bridge365 name is not used in a misleading manner; and
the deployment is not Sold as a standalone software product.
6.5 Circumvention

You may not structure a transaction, service, technical architecture, corporate arrangement, or distribution method primarily for the purpose of avoiding the restrictions in this License.

6.6 Removal of Notices

You may not alter, remove, hide, or obscure:

copyright notices;
license notices;
attribution notices;
notices identifying modifications;
authorship information; or
other legal notices included with the Software.
6.7 Unlawful Use

You may not use the Software in violation of applicable law.

This License does not authorize access to systems, mailboxes, information, personal data, or other resources without the legally required authorization.

7. Distribution and Notices

You may distribute unmodified or modified copies of the Software without charge only if:

the distribution is not a Sale;
every recipient receives a complete copy of this License;
all copyright, attribution, and license notices are retained;
modified copies contain a prominent notice stating that the Software has been modified;
the notice identifies the date of the modification;
You do not imply endorsement by or affiliation with the Licensor; and
the distribution does not form part of a Competing Service.

You may not impose terms on recipients that contradict this License or purport to grant them rights that You do not possess.

