13. Termination and Reinstatement

If You materially violate this License, the rights granted to You under this License terminate automatically.

If the Licensor provides written notice of the violation and You fully cure the violation within 30 calendar days after receiving that notice, Your rights under this License are reinstated retroactively.

If:

You do not cure the violation within that period;
the violation cannot reasonably be cured; or
You commit another material violation after reinstatement,

the Licensor may terminate the rights granted to You permanently by written notice.

Termination does not affect:

rights and remedies accrued before termination;
obligations intended to survive termination;
third-party licenses validly granted before termination, provided that the relevant third party remains compliant with this License; or
the Licensor’s ownership of the Software.

Sections concerning restrictions, attribution, trademarks, patents, warranty disclaimers, limitation of liability, governing law, and interpretation survive termination to the extent legally applicable.

The 30-day cure concept reflects a structure also present in the Elastic License 2.0.

